{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And they did not recognize him</b> at all, and there was no further need for him to disguise himself before them. Our Rabbis said (Yevamot 88a) regarding the reason for the recognition: it is because he left them with his beard unsealed, and they did not recognize him — he had gone out from among them without a full-grown beard, and now they found him with a full-grown beard. Now Issachar and Zebulun are only slightly older than Joseph, but since he recognized the older ones, he recognized all of them. Moreover, he recognized them through his own knowledge that they would come there, while they did not recognize him because they did not set their hearts to the possibility that the slave whom they had sold to the Ishmaelites would be the ruler over the land. And Rabbi Abraham (Ibn Ezra on Genesis 42:7) said: \"וַיַּכִּרֵם\" (\"and he recognized them\") — at first he recognized that they were his brothers, and afterwards he looked at each one and recognized him."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:43:48.941628322Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}